#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192617 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3da4448-71cc-5671-8f32-a9f293ad5054" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "61c51284-18f0-5398-857b-7687228e8df8" :question/math-academy-id "e-7985" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X]$.\n$f(x) = \\dfrac{x^2}{9}, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq 3$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$, we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] &= \\int_{0}^{3}x \\cdot \\frac{x^{2}}{9}dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{3}\\frac{x^{3}}{9}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{x^{4}}{36}\\right|_{0}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192618 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8322a1ba-7608-53de-88d9-e360ca8025cd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "c755eddf-3b0d-5a33-aa13-e6a3f7da4244" :question/math-academy-id "e-7986" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[7X-4]$.\n\n$f(x) = \\dfrac{3x^2}{7}, \\quad 1 < x < 2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[7X-4] = 7 \\textrm E[X] - 4\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$, we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] &= \\int_{S}x \\cdot f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{2}x \\cdot \\frac{3x^{2}}{7}dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{3x^{3}}{7}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{3x^{4}}{28}\\right|_{1}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{45}{28}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[7X - 4] &= 7E[X] - 4 \\\\\n&= 7 \\cdot \\frac{45}{28} - 4 \\\\\n&= \\frac{29}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192619 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b84b8fb-5ad7-5c4f-af44-b6d1dc9310c1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable With a Piecewise PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "3a11b9e3-60c8-57f3-8ec6-4ff378d0db62" :question/math-academy-id "e-7987" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X]$.\n${\\frac{1}{4},\\begin{vmatrix}0 < x < 2 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{3}{4},\\end{vmatrix}2 \\le x \\le 3$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$, we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] &= \\int_{0}^{3}x \\cdot f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{2}x \\cdot f(x)dx + \\int_{2}^{3}x \\cdot f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{2}x \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}dx + \\int_{2}^{3}x \\cdot (\\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{3}{4})dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{2}\\frac{x}{4}dx + \\int_{2}^{3}(\\frac{x^{2}}{2} - \\frac{3x}{4})dx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{x^{2}}{8}\\right|_{0}^{2} + \\left.(\\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{3x^{2}}{8})\\right|_{2}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{31}{24} \\\\\n&= \\frac{43}{24}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193400 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8322a1ba-7608-53de-88d9-e360ca8025cd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "beb8e572-d355-5b9e-9db7-fad6bf9cc428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192328} {:answer/id #uuid "f5523beb-c1ce-57b7-95d3-67749a5266b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192329} {:answer/id #uuid "2e80ca0c-6a04-5c09-9c17-2034f81e97e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192330} {:answer/id #uuid "437fe653-fd9f-53eb-9e04-17a88b8d4bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192331} {:answer/id #uuid "4e170e19-e1b1-5e95-b461-a4cb6c8f7ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192332}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b941308d-d487-55e0-9a91-cc64a7bfa6a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192327}] :question/id #uuid "b6fdbb6b-bf50-55db-8f1b-9ba9143d4ac9" :question/math-academy-id "q-90393" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $E[3X - 4]$.\n\n$f(x) = \\frac{x}{8} - \\frac{1}{4}, 2 < x < 6$"}]}
